i've been a fan of apple's macbook pro  for years now  for various reasons ranging from the  excellent build quality  to the mac os software and it isn't very  common for a windows laptop  to make me disappointed in my macbook  pro  but that's exactly what happened with  the brand new 2020  razer blade stealth 13. so in this video  i'm going to take a look at this laptop  from a macbook user's point of view  since that's what i own and i love and  so far  i'm really impressed from the first time  i unboxed this new razer laptop  i noticed that the build quality felt  very similar to the macbook pro  thanks to the all metal design which is  very solid  my only issue with it is the black  finish which is such a fingerprint  magnet  that i've given up on trying to keep it  looking clean but i absolutely love  the one-handed open hinge which is  something i really enjoy about my  macbook  so good job razer you nailed it on the  build quality front  and to make it even better it supports  windows hello  so it logs you in as soon as you open it  no need to enter a password or touch the  fingerprint sensor  like the macbook pro forces you to do  now with the razer's display open  the keyboard and trackpad layout looks  almost identical to the macbook pro  and i honestly love that about it since  it feels so familiar  as far as the keyboard i like the  keyboard feel better on the razer  since it seems to have more key travel  and a good amount of feedback as well  and one thing that i really don't like  on the macbook pro is the touch bar  i really wish apple never released it  because  the function keys on the blade stealth  are so much better  and it's also nice to see that the razer  gives us customizable rgb keyboard  backlighting as well  as for the trackpad i'm happy to see  razer using up all of the space  available instead of making it smaller  but going from a force touch trackpad on  the macbook  to a traditional diving board style kind  of sucks  but it's still better than a lot of  other windows laptops and i fully  understand that apple has patented the  force touch trackpad  so razer's doing the best with what  they've got now when i compared the  speakers between them  the macbook pro was the clear winner in  terms of sound quality  however the razer packed just as much  volume which is very important to me  when i'm watching  shows or youtube videos so here's a  short clip so you can hear it for  yourself  as far as the ports the razer gives you  the best of both worlds  compared to the macbook pro which  strictly gives you four thunderbolt 3  ports to work with  the razer actually gives you two usb a  ports and two  usb c ports one of which supports  thunderbolt 3  and i find that to be the perfect  combination for any situation  now finally getting into the display  this is where i found  a major downside but also a huge upside  the downside is that the display has a  massive chin  or bottom bezel thanks to razer choosing  to stick to a 16x9 aspect ratio  and once you see this chin you can't  unsee it  and it bothers me every time i look at  it but what i'm very happy about is the  freedom  razer gave us to choose the display we  want  if you want a premium ultrabook but you  want to save some money  you can get the standard 1080p display  and if you're a gamer  you can choose the 120hz display to take  advantage of high frame rate gaming  thanks to that dedicated gtx 1650 ti  graphics card  which i'll get into in a moment and if  you're a creative professional  you can buy the 4k display with  excellent quality  for things like photo and video editing  and it even comes with touch screen  support  this makes the razer blade stealth  perfect for those three markets  so while the large bottom bezel is a bit  disappointing  razer nailed the display options and  with that  let's get into performance i'm happy to  see that this laptop comes loaded with  up-to-date specs like intel's 10th gen  i7 processor  wi-fi 6 16 gigabytes of ram  and the most important part that makes  this  laptop great the dedicated 1650 ti  graphics card this is something you  simply can't get  on any 13-inch macbook so getting such a  good card  and a 1800 premium ultrabook is  impressive just look at the difference  in graphics performance compared to  apple's 2020 13-inch macbook pro  and it's all thanks to the dedicated  graphics it even beat out the 16-inch  macbook  pro in terms of the unigine heaven  gaming benchmark  so i decided to do some gaming on the  razer and i was surprised to see that i  got a pretty smooth and consistent  50-60 fps while playing call of duty war  zone  and that's great for a laptop this thin  and portable  the only downside was that there was a  bit of coil whine in the fan noise which  did get annoying  but i'm sure that it won't bother gamers  much if they're using headphones  and on the flip side for creative  professional work  the razer didn't score as well as the  macbook pro  but it still performed decently well so  for something like video editing  it'll do great i was also very happy to  see that the blade stealth  came with an extremely fast ssd which  was faster than the one on the macbook  pro  which is unusual since macbooks used to  come with much faster ssds  so good job razer basically with  everything i said  going into account if you don't have a  software preference  and you could go with either windows or  mac os then i would honestly say that  the razer blade stealth 13  is the better laptop and the number one  reason for that  is the fact that you cannot get a  dedicated graphics card  on the 13-inch macbook pro so that means  you can't really game on it  without buying an egpu setup and that's  the reason why the small amount of  gaming that i do  happens on my iphone when it could have  been on my macbook pro  if it had more graphics power so that's  what makes the razer so great  since you not only get great performance  for gaming and creative professional  work  but you also get a thin light and  portable design  alongside excellent build quality an  awesome  keyboard and the freedom to choose the  display you need  based on what you do so i think the  mixture of all of that  makes this razor blade stealth worth it  compared to cheaper windows laptops  and i can say with certainty that if i  wasn't attached to the wonderful and  reliable mac os  software that continues to make me favor  my macbook pro  this is honestly the windows laptop that  i would buy  even despite the couple of downsides  like the black finish  and the massive bottom display bezel so  hopefully you guys enjoyed this review  and if this video helped make a decision  on which one to buy  we'll have links to both of these  laptops down in the description below  and if you like this t-shirt you can  find it just below this video  thanks for watching and click that  circle above to subscribe for more  videos like this one  [Music]
 

